* ============================================================================
* workspace_scope_regression.dts
*
* AIF-078 stage 3. WORKSPACE CLOSE IS SCOPED TO A WORKSPACE.
*
* WHAT CHANGED AND WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
*   Until stage 3, WORKSPACE CLOSE ran
*       for (int area0 = 0; area0 < xbase::MAX_AREA; ++area0)
*   and was correct only because exactly one workspace had ever existed. The
*   owner named it directly: "close_all needs to be SCOPED to a specific
*   workspace instead of 0-max_areas. workspaces have to know the group of
*   areas that belong to them." Stage 2 built that group and proved it (14
*   tables opened, 14 members, 0 after close, measured 2026-08-22). This is
*   the first spec that can tell the two implementations apart.
*
*   WS_T1 IS THAT DISCRIMINATOR. Under the old sweep it goes RED: closing a
*   child workspace took every area in the process with it, DEFAULT's included.
*   Under the scoped close it goes green. Delete the scoping and this file
*   reds on exactly one line.
*
* THE COST ARGUMENT, WHICH IS NOT SECONDARY
*   MAX_AREA is 512 for testing and the owner has stated the real ceiling is
*   not 512 -- "can you imagine how long it would take to give you a dotscript
*   results of a 10 trillion max_area pass." A close that is O(MAX_AREA) does
*   not survive that sentence. A close that is O(members) does not care what
*   MAX_AREA is. WS_T1 defends the correctness; the cost follows from the same
*   change.
*
* SET RECURSION, AND WHY BOTH ARMS ARE HERE
*   Owner ruling 2026-08-22: "we need a SET RECURSION ON | OFF / even with OFF
*   we still allow multiple workspaces, just parallel." So the flag does NOT
*   gate whether nesting may exist -- it gates whether an operation DESCENDS.
*   WS_T2 is the arm where that is load-bearing: same script, same shape, one
*   flag flipped, and the nested workspace's table is still readable afterward.
*   Without WS_T2 the OFF branch would be a documented preference rather than a
*   measured behaviour.
*
* WHAT THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT ASSERT, AND WHY
*   That a workspace closed under RECURSION ON is EMPTY. USE_AGAIN established
*   the rule the hard way, over three cuts: NO MARKER IN THIS LANGUAGE CAN
*   ASSERT THAT AN AREA IS EMPTY, because the marker evaluator binds a null
*   area unless the area is OPEN (rhs_eval.cpp:969) -- being closed is the very
*   thing under assertion -- and an errored marker PRINTS NOTHING rather than
*   going red, so a green count still reads full while a claim has silently
*   left the suite. So the recursive close is proven by CONTRAST (WS_T2's
*   survival under OFF against its absence under ON) and by the member counts
*   in the two WORKSPACE REGISTRY blocks, which are read from the transcript.
*   That is external measurement, the IDXDIFF precedent: "a .dts cannot count
*   engine trace output."
*
* MARKERS ARE FIELD-VALUE COMPARISONS, every one of them. A spec that asserts
*   SHAPE passes green on a blanked table -- the FIELDMGR_APPEND doctrine.
*
* Self-bootstrapping: creates WSDEF / WSPAR / WSCHI in SANDBOX and erases them.
* Never touches a live fixture. Leaves three runtime-only workspaces declared
* (WSPARENT, WSCHILD) -- they hold no areas and do not survive a restart.
* Restores SET RECURSION ON at the end.
*   Standalone:  DO workspace_scope_regression
*   Regression:  REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_SCOPE
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX

FORMULA "WORKSPACE-SCOPE-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- clean slate -------------------------------------------------------------
* CLOSE ALL, not bare CLOSE: this must be the everywhere form regardless of
* which workspace a previous script left current.
SET RECURSION ON
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
ERASE wsdef CONFIRM
ERASE wspar CONFIRM
ERASE wschi CONFIRM

* --- three sentinels, one per workspace --------------------------------------
* Each lands in its OWN engine area, because CREATE closes the current area
* before writing -- creating into an area that already holds a sentinel would
* destroy the thing under test. The engine slot is chosen explicitly rather
* than inherited.
SELECT 0
CREATE X64 WSDEF (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "DEF"

WORKSPACE NEW WSPARENT
WORKSPACE NEW WSCHILD UNDER WSPARENT

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSPARENT
SELECT 1
CREATE X64 WSPAR (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 2
REPLACE MARK WITH "PAR"

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSCHILD
SELECT 2
CREATE X64 WSCHI (ID N(4), MARK C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 3
REPLACE MARK WITH "CHI"

* --- G0/G1/G2: the fixture is real before anything is closed -----------------
* Guards for everything below. A green WS_T1 means nothing if the sentinel it
* reads was never written.
SELECT 0
GO TOP
? "WS_G0_default_sentinel_written:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "DEF")
SELECT 1
GO TOP
? "WS_G1_parent_sentinel_written:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "PAR")
SELECT 2
GO TOP
? "WS_G2_child_sentinel_written:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "CHI")

* --- the tree, before ---------------------------------------------------------
* Expect: DEFAULT parent 0 depth 0 members 1
*         WSPARENT parent 0 depth 0 members 1
*         WSCHILD  parent <WSPARENT> depth 1 members 1
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

* --- ARM 1: RECURSION ON -- close the parent ---------------------------------
* Closes WSCHILD's areas first (post-order), then WSPARENT's. DEFAULT is not
* named and must not be touched.
SET RECURSION ON
WORKSPACE SWITCH WSPARENT
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- the tree, after ----------------------------------------------------------
* Expect WSPARENT members 0 and WSCHILD members 0, DEFAULT members 1. These
* counts are the direct evidence that the recursion descended; the markers
* below are the indirect evidence. Read both.
WORKSPACE REGISTRY

* --- WS_T1: THE DISCRIMINATOR -------------------------------------------------
* DEFAULT's sentinel survived a close of a DIFFERENT workspace. Under the old
* 0..MAX_AREA sweep this area was closed too and this line goes red.
SELECT 0
GO TOP
? "WS_T1_scoped_close_spared_default:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "DEF")

* --- ARM 2: RECURSION OFF -- close the parent, child must survive -------------
* Rebuild the same shape. The workspaces still exist with zero members, so only
* the tables are reopened.
SET RECURSION OFF

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSPARENT
SELECT 1
USE wspar

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSCHILD
SELECT 2
USE wschi

* Guard the rebuild before asserting anything about it.
SELECT 2
GO TOP
? "WS_G3_child_reopened:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "CHI")

WORKSPACE SWITCH WSPARENT
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- WS_T2: OFF LEFT THE NESTED WORKSPACE OPEN --------------------------------
* The flag is load-bearing here and nowhere else. Under RECURSION ON this same
* sequence closes area 2; under OFF it must not, and the close must have SAID
* so ("SET RECURSION is OFF; 1 nested workspace(s) ... were left open").
SELECT 2
GO TOP
? "WS_T2_recursion_off_kept_child_open:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "CHI")

* --- WS_T3: DEFAULT is untouched under either flag ----------------------------
SELECT 0
GO TOP
? "WS_T3_default_untouched_under_off:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "DEF")

* --- ARM 3: CLOSE ALL still means everywhere ----------------------------------
* The old bare-CLOSE contract did not disappear, it moved to an explicit form.
* Nothing may be left open after this, including the workspace nobody named.
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL

* --- WS_T4: the files were RELEASED, not merely forgotten ---------------------
* Reopening and reading proves the close reached the filesystem. A close that
* dropped its bookkeeping while leaving handles open would pass every marker
* above and fail here.
SELECT 0
USE wsdef
GO TOP
? "WS_T4_close_all_released_the_file:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "DEF")

* --- teardown -----------------------------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
ERASE wsdef CONFIRM
ERASE wspar CONFIRM
ERASE wschi CONFIRM

* Restore the shipped default. ERRORSTOP is the cautionary precedent: a spec
* that leaves a global flag flipped poisons every script after it in the suite.
SET RECURSION ON
WORKSPACE SWITCH DEFAULT

FORMULA "WORKSPACE-SCOPE-PROOF-END"
